course: dictionary
lesson: 8105
title: Renew: make it last, start again, make it new
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Renew is a verb, so it is something you do. It has three meanings, and the words around it tell you which one. «Renew a library book» means make the loan last longer, so you can keep the book for more time.
explain: «Renew a friendship» means start it again after a break. «Renew the paint» means make something look new and fresh again. Always ask: what is being renewed, and what would fit here?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «make it last longer» fits «renew the book», you have the right meaning. If it does not fit, try another meaning until the sentence makes sense.
fact: Renew means to make something last longer, to start something again after a break, or to make something new or fresh again.
fact: Renewed and renewing are other forms of renew, and renewable means able to renew itself.
fact: «Renewable» energy comes from sources that renew themselves, such as sunlight and wind, which come every day.
fact: Some resources, such as wood or fish, can renew themselves if they are used carefully, but oil and metals do not come back once they are used up.
fact: Coal, oil and gas formed over millions of years, so once we burn them they are gone for good.
exercise: «Renew the paint» on the old fence means what? | *To make it look new and fresh again | To spill it on the grass | To count the tins | To throw the paint away
exercise: At the library, «renew a book» means what? | To read it aloud to the class | To return it at once | To lose it for ever | *To keep it for longer
exercise: Which of these renews itself? | Metals | *Sunlight | Oil | Coal
test: «A free trial often renews into a paid subscription automatically unless you cancel it in time.» What does renews mean here? | Gets lost in the post | *Continues automatically for another period | Ends at once with no money | Is given away for free
test: «Forests, fish and soil renew themselves only if people do not use them faster than they grow back.» What must people do? | Use them faster than they grow back | Burn them all at once | Forget them for years | *Use them no faster than they grow back
exam: «Others do not renew in a human lifetime: coal, oil and gas formed from plants and tiny sea creatures.» Which resources do not renew in a human lifetime? | Trees planted in a forest | Sunlight and wind | *Coal, oil and gas | Wood and fish
